"NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription" = "Location is used only while the app is open: to suggest the nearest station on the main screen; during a trip, to refine the train's position on above-ground metro sections; in Calibration mode, which you turn on yourself, to save a track of the ride to a file on your device. For the station reminder, iOS itself watches the station area: the app never sees your location. The app never uses location in the background and never transmits it anywhere.";
"NSMotionUsageDescription" = "The accelerometer is recorded only in Calibration mode, which you turn on yourself; the data stays on your device.";
"CFBundleDisplayName" = "Metro Timer";
"NSAlarmKitUsageDescription" = "The alarm rings one stop before your station, even in silent mode. It is on only when you turn it on in the trip screen.";
